# MeetUp API — Project Stack & Architecture

## Stack
- .NET 10 + ASP.NET Core Web API (controllers) + Entity Framework Core
- Database: MySQL via `Pomelo.EntityFrameworkCore.MySql`
- Tests: xUnit + Moq + FluentAssertions (unit) | WebApplicationFactory + SQLite in-memory (integration)
- **SQLite in-memory is used ONLY in tests — never in the application**
- Configuration via `appsettings.json` + environment variables (`ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection`)

## Layered Architecture
```
Controller → Service → Repository (class + interface, DbContext underneath)
```
- Controllers handle HTTP only — no business logic
- Services own all business rules
- Repositories are classes with interfaces that encapsulate the `DbContext` — no LINQ queries in services

## Naming
- Class names and method names: **English** for classes, domain verbs may stay in Portuguese when mirroring the ubiquitous language (`CriarEvento`, `Inscrever`)
- Domain attribute names in DTOs (request/response): **Portuguese** (`titulo`, `descricao`, `dataHora`, `local`, `limiteVagas`)
- Entity properties: **English**, mapped to Portuguese columns/tables via `HasColumnName`/`ToTable` in `OnModelCreating`

```csharp
// ✅ Entity property in English → column in Portuguese (OnModelCreating)
builder.Property(e => e.Title).HasColumnName("titulo").IsRequired();

// ✅ DTO attribute in Portuguese (serialized as camelCase JSON: titulo, dataHora)
public record EventRequest([Required] string Titulo, string Descricao, [Required] DateTime DataHora);
```

## Other rules
- DTOs are C# `record`s — no boilerplate classes with getters/setters
- Entities have explicit constructors (parameterless + full) — no records for entities
- Validation with DataAnnotations (`[Required]`, `[EmailAddress]`, `[Range]`) + ModelState
- Centralized error handling in an exception middleware — never try/catch in controllers
- Dependency injection by constructor, registered in `Program.cs`
- All API responses are JSON with semantic HTTP status codes
